13:03.533 --> 13:05.242
Sensei Dan, he's using a sword!

13:05.243 --> 13:07.537
No swords, guys.

13:14.377 --> 13:17.129
Brian, are you sure
about getting neutered?

13:17.130 --> 13:19.923
I am. You've seen everything
George Townshend's accomplished.

13:19.924 --> 13:21.675
That's the life I've always dreamed of.

13:21.676 --> 13:24.094
Yes, but how much
do you really know about him?

13:24.095 --> 13:26.430
- Have you read his books?
- Of course I've read his books.

13:26.431 --> 13:27.973
They changed my life.

13:27.974 --> 13:29.891
Look, Stewie,
this is a huge step for me,

13:29.892 --> 13:31.476
and if you can't support me,

13:31.477 --> 13:34.105
well, then maybe I should
cut you out of my life, too.

13:35.231 --> 13:36.898
Brian, that's a closet.

13:36.899 --> 13:38.901
I know. I have stuff to do in here.

13:50.371 --> 13:52.289
Well, nothing left to do but binge-watch

13:52.290 --> 13:54.958
<i>- Ken Burns' History of Jazz.
- What?</i>

13:54.959 --> 13:57.836
<i>The rhythmic drums of the Congo.</i>

13:57.837 --> 14:01.590
<i>300 years later, Charlie Bird Parker.</i>

14:01.591 --> 14:03.425
<i>But how did we get there?</i>

14:10.391 --> 14:12.642
Lois, what are you doing here?

14:12.643 --> 14:15.103
Did someone die?
Do I get to go home early?

14:15.104 --> 14:18.440
Well, Peter, since you were
having that jeans fun,

14:18.441 --> 14:20.859
I thought it might be fun
to come by and sell

14:20.860 --> 14:24.196
some of my homemade jewelry
to your coworkers during lunch.

14:24.197 --> 14:26.531
What? Lois, you can't do that.

14:26.532 --> 14:28.617
Once a guy's wife sells
something in the break room,

14:28.618 --> 14:30.285
no one ever looks at him the same.

14:30.286 --> 14:32.287
Two years ago,
Bentley's wife made him hang

14:32.288 --> 14:34.664
a sign-up sheet
to sponsor her in an AIDS walk,

14:34.665 --> 14:36.166
and we've hated him ever since.

14:36.167 --> 14:37.571
Don't look at me, Bentley.

14:38.586 --> 14:40.212
Well, Peter, all you have to do

14:40.213 --> 14:42.297
is say you like my haircut,
and I'll leave.

14:42.298 --> 14:44.424
- Never.
- Suit yourself.

14:44.425 --> 14:47.385
Everyone, I'm Peter Griffin's wife.

14:47.386 --> 14:49.638
I took a jewelry-making class last month

14:49.639 --> 14:51.640
with a group of preschool moms,

14:51.641 --> 14:54.310
and now I'm gonna do it as a career.

15:01.692 --> 15:04.027
Hey, you want a half of my sandwich?

15:04.028 --> 15:05.987
Oh. Yeah. Very cool, Bentley.

15:05.988 --> 15:08.198
- Who made this?
- My wife.

15:08.199 --> 15:10.826
- Oh, y-your wife with AIDS?
- She doesn't have AIDS.

15:10.827 --> 15:13.078
<i>She did a walk for people with AIDS.</i>

15:13.079 --> 15:15.914
But presumably there were people
who had AIDS at the walk?

15:15.915 --> 15:17.374
Yeah, but you can't get...

15:17.375 --> 15:19.210
Yeah, it's a no
on the sandwich, Bentley.

15:22.922 --> 15:24.464
Greetings, Lois.

15:24.465 --> 15:26.591
Oh, my God, Peter,
you're gonna make me vomit.

15:26.592 --> 15:28.510
I'm just getting in some 'cize.

15:28.511 --> 15:31.347
That's what I call exercise now: 'Cize.

15:34.934 --> 15:36.852
Oh, God, Peter, please put that thing

15:36.853 --> 15:38.478
in the garage and change your clothes.

15:38.479 --> 15:39.855
Oh, I'd be happy to, Lois.

15:39.856 --> 15:41.523
But I'm not doing it because you said.

15:41.524 --> 15:43.525
I'm doing it because of
the mean seventh graders

15:43.526 --> 15:45.694
who have been chucking
footballs at me all day.

15:45.695 --> 15:48.864
There he is! Let's get that fat dork!

15:48.865 --> 15:50.782
I'm home! Home is safe!

15:50.783 --> 15:53.244
Home is safe!

15:58.916 --> 16:02.210
I see you found all of
George Townshend's books.

16:02.211 --> 16:03.545
That was fast.

16:03.546 --> 16:05.505
Yep, got my own system.

16:05.506 --> 16:07.716
I call it "The Stewie Decimal System."

16:09.760 --> 16:13.555
Oh, Stewie, you're gonna make me
spit out my saltwater taffy.

16:16.350 --> 16:18.584
Oh, my God!

16:18.585 --> 16:20.061
Brian's in trouble!

16:20.062 --> 16:23.190
Stewie, I've got to have you
around here more often.

16:23.191 --> 16:26.832
Oh, I think you'll
find me here... periodically.

16:27.904 --> 16:30.531
There's homeless sperm on this.

16:37.788 --> 16:39.956
- Where are the glasses?
- I moved them.

16:39.957 --> 16:41.208
What? Why?

16:41.209 --> 16:42.417
I moved everything.

16:42.418 --> 16:44.753
All the glasses, the bowls, the plates.

16:44.754 --> 16:47.528
Nothing is where it's been
for the past 17 years.

16:47.529 --> 16:48.589
Nothing.

16:50.927 --> 16:52.761
I'm gonna become a deejay.

16:52.762 --> 16:55.555
I'm going to hire a life coach.

16:55.556 --> 16:57.641
I'm gonna make one political donation

16:57.642 --> 17:00.435
with your e-mail address
so you'll be screwed for life.

17:00.436 --> 17:03.563
I'm going to rededicate
my life to Christ.

17:03.564 --> 17:04.981
Oh, that's really bad.

17:04.982 --> 17:07.317
I'm gonna start a podcast
that has no focus

17:07.318 --> 17:09.694
and it'll take up
an inordinate amount of time.

17:09.695 --> 17:12.614
I'm going to constantly complain
about my fibromyalgia.

17:12.615 --> 17:15.116
- You don't have fibromyalgia.
- No one does!

17:15.117 --> 17:18.203
Every time a waiter tells me
their name, I'm gonna use it.

17:18.204 --> 17:21.790
I'm gonna get really into
Halloween, like, really into it!

17:21.791 --> 17:24.125
Gross. I'm gonna wear a denim shirt

17:24.126 --> 17:26.169
with the Looney Tunes guys
embroidered on it

17:26.170 --> 17:28.005
to church every Sunday.

17:31.384 --> 17:33.636
Oh, Peter. Oh, Peter.

17:37.807 --> 17:41.476
So, what do you think of my haircut now?

17:41.477 --> 17:43.354
It's ugly. I hate it.

17:48.943 --> 17:51.319
- How you feeling, buddy?
- Good.

17:51.320 --> 17:53.571
Nervous but strangely excited.

17:53.572 --> 17:55.865
I haven't been totally honest with you.

17:55.866 --> 17:57.325
I was never neutered.

17:57.326 --> 17:58.910
But you're about to be.

17:58.911 --> 18:00.328
What? No!

18:00.329 --> 18:02.163
Save me, Sensei Dan!

18:02.164 --> 18:04.959
No neutering, guys.

18:11.799 --> 18:13.008
Why are you doing this?

18:13.009 --> 18:14.676
What did I do to you that was so bad?

18:14.677 --> 18:16.136
You abandoned me.

18:16.137 --> 18:18.513
You promised we'd be there
for each other forever.

18:18.514 --> 18:20.432
Then the minute
Peter Griffin came along,

18:20.433 --> 18:22.183
you just got in his car and left me.

18:22.184 --> 18:24.602
I was gonna come back
and get you, and-and then,

18:24.603 --> 18:27.105
and then Trump happened
and-and all that...

18:27.106 --> 18:28.273
Liar!

18:28.274 --> 18:30.233
I've wanted to cut
your balls off for years,

18:30.234 --> 18:32.610
but the fact that you're
choosing to do it yourself

18:32.611 --> 18:34.529
is so much more satisfying.

18:34.530 --> 18:36.614
But I'm not choosing to do it myself.

18:36.615 --> 18:37.910
I love my balls.

18:37.911 --> 18:40.328
They smell awful.

18:54.925 --> 18:56.551
Stay back!

18:56.552 --> 18:59.929
Stewie. Y-You saved me.

18:59.930 --> 19:01.598
Oh.

19:01.599 --> 19:03.892
- Well, almost.
- What is it?

19:03.893 --> 19:05.727
Oh, my God, they got one!

19:05.728 --> 19:07.729
Or you still have one.

19:07.730 --> 19:10.065
Maybe you should be
a scrotum half-full guy.

19:10.066 --> 19:11.816
How did you know what he was doing?

19:11.817 --> 19:13.943
I read his book.

19:13.944 --> 19:15.904
"There is no greater motivation

19:15.905 --> 19:18.031
"than the destruction of an enemy,

19:18.032 --> 19:20.658
"and my enemy is Brian Griffin.

19:20.659 --> 19:23.828
"One day, I will convince him
to cut off his own balls,

19:23.829 --> 19:26.581
and that will be
my greatest accomplishment."

19:26.582 --> 19:28.750
You said his books changed your life,

19:28.751 --> 19:30.418
but you didn't even read them.

19:30.419 --> 19:32.587
This is why you're nothing.

19:32.588 --> 19:34.126
I'm sorry, okay?

19:34.127 --> 19:35.507
Yes, I abandoned you.

19:35.508 --> 19:37.467
And I didn't go back to find you.

19:37.468 --> 19:39.260
I'm a bad friend, I admit it.

19:39.261 --> 19:41.721
But did you ever think
that you should be thanking me?

19:41.722 --> 19:43.807
Thanking you? For what?

19:43.808 --> 19:45.392
For everything you have.

19:45.393 --> 19:48.770
Your hatred for me is what
motivated you your whole life.

19:48.771 --> 19:51.356
Without me, none of this
would've been possible.

19:51.357 --> 19:52.650
I made you.

19:54.151 --> 19:55.944
You've already got one of my balls.

19:55.945 --> 19:56.986
Isn't that enough?

19:56.987 --> 19:59.114
You know what, Brian?

19:59.115 --> 20:00.824
It is enough.

20:00.825 --> 20:03.201
You'll probably keep it
in a trophy case or something.

20:03.202 --> 20:05.161
Oh, no. I ate it already.

20:05.162 --> 20:06.996
Dogs are gross.

20:10.251 --> 20:12.794
Thank you, Stewie. You really saved me.

20:12.795 --> 20:14.838
My pleasure, Brian.

20:14.839 --> 20:17.215
Well, the good news is
we can give you a prosthetic.

20:17.216 --> 20:18.842
The bad news is

20:18.843 --> 20:21.928
it's one of the bells
from a jester's hat.

20:21.929 --> 20:23.471
There's no brain activity,

20:23.472 --> 20:25.640
so we're gonna harvest his bells.

20:25.641 --> 20:27.225
We understand.

20:27.226 --> 20:28.643
Why did the king

20:28.644 --> 20:31.647
have to hit him so hard?!

20:38.737 --> 20:42.031
So, anyone want to ask me about my week?

20:42.032 --> 20:45.077
Kind of a big week for the Megster.

20:46.245 --> 20:48.872
Big envelope in the mail.

20:48.873 --> 20:51.666
Yep, early admittance.

20:51.667 --> 20:54.043
Day one, August 26, clean slate.

20:54.044 --> 20:55.378
Closing credits.

20:55.379 --> 20:57.755
Congratulations on Bowdoin, Meg!

20:57.756 --> 21:00.550
- Closing credits!
- Oh, we're done?